:name: oveRTOS CMocka suite on Zephyr/STM32F746 — heap mode
:description: Boot the oveRTOS test firmware on Zephyr's stm32f746g_disco target under Renode's stm32f7_discovery-bb platform; capture stdout via USART1 + a semihosting UART.

using sysbus

$bin?=@output/tests/renode-stm32f746-zephyr/zephyr/zephyr.elf

mach create "stm32f746"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/stm32f7_discovery-bb.repl

sysbus LoadELF $bin

# Zephyr's stm32f746g_disco defconfig routes printk through USART1
# (the Discovery's ST-Link VCP).  Renode models that as STM32F7_USART —
# tap its TX into a file so the outer harness can grep for the CMocka
# summary post-run.  Semihosting traps for `semihosting_exit` go
# through the CPU debug interface (CONFIG_SEMIHOST=y in prj.conf), no
# UART backend required.
$uart_out?=@/tmp/renode-stm32f746-zephyr.uart
sysbus.usart1 CreateFileBackend $uart_out true
showAnalyzer sysbus.usart1

$rlog?=@/tmp/renode-stm32f746-zephyr.renode.log
logFile $rlog

# Zephyr's STM32F7 boot sequence takes longer simulated time than the
# FreeRTOS sibling (PLL bring-up, devicetree-driven init, kernel
# scheduler).  10 simulated seconds is enough for the full common
# suite — the test summary lands around 4.5s of sim time — and keeps
# wall-clock under the harness's 300s ceiling.
emulation RunFor "00:00:10"
